  "notes": "Means to start operating or get moving. Used for both machines/engines and figurative 'launches' of projects and initiatives.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- エンジンが{始動|しどう}する — the engine starts\n- エンジンを{始動|しどう}させる — to start the engine\n- プロジェクトが{始動|しどう}する — a project launches\n- {本格的|ほんかくてき}に{始動|しどう}する — to get fully underway\n- {始動|しどう}が{遅|おく}れる — the start is delayed\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {起動|きどう}する — to boot up, start (especially computers/systems)\n- {発動|はつどう}する — to invoke, activate (laws, powers)\n- {始|はじ}まる — to begin (general, everyday)\n- {開始|かいし}する — to commence (formal)\n\nUSAGE:\n{始動|しどう} is more concrete and dynamic than {開始|かいし}. It evokes the image of an engine turning over — the physical start of something. {開始|かいし} is more neutral and administrative.",
